+  tip_239: agent.api_max_retries (default 3) controls how many times the agent retries a failed API call before surfacing the error — lower it for fast fallback.
+  tip_240: The gateway caches AIAgent instances per session — destroying this cache breaks Anthropic prompt caching.
+  tip_241: Any website can expose skills via /.well-known/skills/index.json — the skills hub discovers them automatically.
+  tip_242: The skills audit log at ~/.hermes/skills/.hub/audit.log tracks every install and removal operation.
+  tip_243: 'Stale git worktrees are auto-cleaned on startup: clean, fully-merged trees get pruned; dirty or unpushed work is always preserved.'
+  tip_244: Profiles scope Hermes state via HERMES_HOME; host tool subprocesses keep your real HOME unless terminal.home_mode is profile.
+  tip_245: HERMES_HOME_MODE env var (octal, e.g. 0701) sets custom directory permissions for web server traversal.
+  tip_246: 'Container mode: place .container-mode in HERMES_HOME and the host CLI auto-execs into the container.'
+  tip_247: 'Ctrl+C has 5 priority tiers: cancel recording → cancel prompts → cancel picker → interrupt agent → exit.'
+  tip_248: Every interrupt during an agent run is logged to ~/.hermes/interrupt_debug.log with timestamps.
+  tip_249: BROWSER_CDP_URL connects browser tools to any running Chromium-family browser — accepts WebSocket, HTTP, or host:port.
+  tip_250: BROWSERBASE_ADVANCED_STEALTH=true enables advanced anti-detection with custom Chromium (Scale Plan).
+  tip_251: The CLI auto-switches to compact mode in terminals narrower than 80 columns.
+  tip_252: 'Quick commands support two types: exec (run shell command directly) and alias (redirect to another command).'
+  tip_253: 'Per-task delegation model: delegation.model and delegation.provider in config route subagents to cheaper models.'
+  tip_254: delegation.reasoning_effort independently controls thinking depth for subagents.
+  tip_255: 'display.platforms in config.yaml allows per-platform display overrides: {telegram: {tool_progress: all}}.'
+  tip_256: human_delay.mode in config simulates human typing speed — configurable min_ms/max_ms range.
+  tip_257: Config version migrations run automatically on load — new config keys appear without manual intervention.
+  tip_258: GPT and Codex models get special system prompt guidance for tool discipline and mandatory tool use.
+  tip_259: Gemini models get tailored directives for absolute paths, parallel tool calls, and non-interactive commands.
+  tip_260: context.engine in config.yaml can be set to a plugin name for alternative context management strategies.
+  tip_261: Browser page snapshots over 15,000 characters are truncated or auto-summarized; the full snapshot is saved to cache/web for read_file paging.
+  tip_262: 'The compressor does a cheap pre-pass: tool outputs over 200 chars are replaced with placeholders before the LLM runs.'
+  tip_263: When compression fails, further attempts are paused for 10 minutes to avoid API hammering.
+  tip_264: Long dangerous commands (>70 chars) get a 'view' option in the approval prompt to see the full text first.
+  tip_265: Audio level visualization shows ▁▂▃▄▅▆▇ bars during voice recording based on microphone RMS levels.
+  tip_266: Profile names cannot collide with existing PATH binaries — 'hermes profile create ls' would be rejected.
+  tip_267: hermes profile create backup --clone-all copies everything (config, keys, SOUL.md, memories, skills, sessions).
+  tip_268: The voice record key is configurable via voice.record_key in config.yaml — not just Ctrl+B.
+  tip_269: .cursorrules and .cursor/rules/*.mdc files are auto-detected and loaded as project context.
+  tip_270: Context files support 10+ prompt injection patterns — invisible Unicode, 'ignore instructions', exfil attempts.
+  tip_271: GPT-5 and Codex use 'developer' role instead of 'system' in the message format.
+  tip_272: 'Per-task auxiliary overrides: auxiliary.vision.provider, auxiliary.compression.model, etc. in config.yaml.'
+  tip_273: The auxiliary client treats 'main' as a provider alias — resolves to your actual primary provider + model.
+  tip_274: hermes claw migrate --dry-run previews OpenClaw migration without writing anything.
+  tip_275: File paths pasted with quotes or escaped spaces are handled automatically — no manual cleanup needed.
+  tip_276: Slash commands never trigger the large-paste collapse — /command with big arguments works correctly.
+  tip_277: In interrupt mode, slash commands typed during agent execution bypass interrupt logic and run immediately.
+  tip_278: HERMES_DEV=1 bypasses container mode detection for local development.
+  tip_279: Each MCP server gets its own toolset (mcp-servername) that can be toggled independently via hermes tools.
+  tip_280: MCP ${ENV_VAR} placeholders in config are resolved at server spawn — including vars from ~/.hermes/.env.
+  tip_281: Skills from trusted repos (NousResearch) get a 'trusted' security level; community skills get extra scanning.
+  tip_282: The skills quarantine at ~/.hermes/skills/.hub/quarantine/ holds skills pending security review.
+  tip_283: /steer <prompt> injects a note after the next tool call — nudge direction mid-task without interrupting.
+  tip_284: /goal <text> sets a standing Ralph-loop objective — Hermes auto-continues turn after turn until a judge says done.
+  tip_285: /snapshot create [label] saves a full state snapshot of Hermes config; /snapshot restore <id> reverts later.
+  tip_286: /copy [N] copies the last assistant response to your clipboard, or the Nth-from-last with a number.
+  tip_287: /redraw forces a full UI repaint, fixing terminal drift after tmux resize or mouse selection artifacts.
+  tip_288: /agents (alias /tasks) shows active agents and running background tasks across the current session.
+  tip_289: /footer toggles the gateway footer on final replies showing model, context %, and cwd.
+  tip_290: /busy queue|steer|interrupt controls what pressing Enter does while Hermes is working.
+  tip_291: /topic in Telegram DMs enables user-managed multi-session topic mode — /topic <id> restores past sessions inline.
+  tip_292: /approve session|always runs a pending dangerous command with your chosen trust scope; /deny rejects it.
+  tip_293: /restart gracefully restarts the gateway after draining active runs, then pings the requester when back up.
+  tip_294: /kanban boards switch <slug> changes the active multi-project Kanban board from inside chat.
+  tip_295: /reload reloads ~/.hermes/.env into the running session — pick up new API keys without restarting.
+  tip_296: cronjob with no_agent=True runs a script on schedule and sends its stdout directly — zero tokens, zero LLM.
+  tip_297: An empty cron script stdout means silent tick — nothing is delivered, perfect for threshold watchdogs.
+  tip_298: HERMES_CRON_MAX_PARALLEL (default 4) caps how many cron jobs run per tick so bursts don't saturate your keys.
+  tip_299: Gateway hooks live under ~/.hermes/hooks/<name>/ with HOOK.yaml + handler.py — handler must be named `handle`.
+  tip_300: Hook events include gateway:startup, session:start, agent:step, and command:* wildcard subscriptions.
+  tip_301: Drop a ~/.hermes/BOOT.md checklist and a gateway:startup hook runs it as a one-shot agent every boot.
+  tip_302: hermes curator run --dry-run previews what the curator would archive or consolidate without mutating anything.
+  tip_303: hermes curator pin <skill> hard-fences a skill against both auto-archival and the agent's skill_manage tool.
+  tip_304: hermes curator rollback restores skills from a pre-run snapshot — backups live under skills/.curator_backups/.
+  tip_305: hermes auth reset <provider> [target] clears cooldowns and exhaustion flags on a whole credential pool, or on one credential by index, id, or label.
+  tip_306: 'credential_pool_strategies.<provider>: round_robin cycles keys evenly instead of the fill_first default.'
+  tip_307: 'use_gateway: true per-tool routes web, image, tts, or browser through your Nous subscription — no extra keys.'
+  tip_308: 'provider_routing.data_collection: deny excludes data-storing providers on OpenRouter.'
+  tip_309: 'provider_routing.require_parameters: true only routes to providers that support every param in your request.'
+  tip_310: HERMES_TUI_RESUME=1 auto-re-attaches to the most recent TUI session on launch — handy after SSH drops.
+  tip_311: HERMES_TUI_THEME=light|dark|<hex> forces the TUI theme on terminals that don't set COLORFGBG.
+  tip_312: Ctrl+G or Ctrl+X Ctrl+E in the TUI opens the input buffer in $EDITOR for long multi-line prompts.
+  tip_313: The TUI renders LaTeX inline — $E=mc^2$ becomes Unicode math instead of raw TeX.
+  tip_314: hermes dashboard launches a local web UI at 127.0.0.1:9119 — zero data leaves localhost.
+  tip_315: hermes dashboard embeds the full Hermes TUI in your browser via xterm.js and a WebSocket PTY.
+  tip_316: Drop a YAML in ~/.hermes/dashboard-themes/ with two palette colors to reskin the entire dashboard.
+  tip_317: 'Dashboard plugins are drop-in: manifest.json + JS bundle in ~/.hermes/dashboard-plugins/ — no npm build required.'
+  tip_318: 'layoutVariant: cockpit in a dashboard theme adds a 260px left rail that plugins can populate via the sidebar slot.'
+  tip_319: 'display.tool_progress_command: true exposes /verbose on messaging platforms; it''s CLI-only by default.'
+  tip_320: HERMES_BACKGROUND_NOTIFICATIONS=result only pings when background tasks finish (vs concise/all/error/off).
+  tip_321: 'HERMES_WRITE_SAFE_ROOT restricts write_file/patch to directory prefixes; multiple paths via os.pathsep (: or ;).'
+  tip_322: HERMES_IGNORE_RULES skips auto-injection of AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, .cursorrules, memory, and preloaded skills.
+  tip_323: HERMES_ACCEPT_HOOKS auto-approves unseen shell hooks declared in config.yaml without a TTY prompt.
+  tip_324: auxiliary.goal_judge.model routes the /goal judge to a cheap fast model to keep loop cost near zero.
+  tip_325: Checkpoints skip directories with more than 50,000 files to avoid slow git operations on massive monorepos.
+  tip_326: 'tts.provider: piper runs 44-language local TTS on CPU — voices auto-download to ~/.hermes/cache/piper-voices/.'
+  tip_327: 'tts.providers.<name>.type: command wires any CLI TTS engine with {input_path} and {output_path} placeholders.'
+  tip_328: API_SERVER_ENABLED=true runs an OpenAI-compatible endpoint alongside the gateway for Open WebUI and LibreChat.
+  tip_329: 'GATEWAY_PROXY_URL runs a split setup: platform I/O locally, agent work delegated to a remote API server.'
+  tip_330: MATRIX_DEVICE_ID pins a stable device ID for E2EE — without it, keys rotate every start and historic decrypt breaks.
+  tip_331: TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET is required whenever TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_URL is set — generate with openssl rand -hex 32.
+  tip_332: batch_runner.py --resume content-matches completed prompts by text so dataset reorders don't re-run finished work.
+  tip_333: /new starts a fresh session in place (alias /reset) — fresh session ID, clean history, CLI stays open.
+  tip_334: /clear wipes the terminal screen AND starts a new session — one shortcut for a visual reset.
+  tip_335: /history prints the current conversation in-line without leaving the CLI — useful for a quick re-read.
+  tip_336: /save writes the current conversation to disk without ending the session.
+  tip_337: '/status shows session info at a glance: ID, title, model, token usage, and elapsed time.'
+  tip_338: /image <path> attaches a local image file for your next prompt without pasting or drag-and-drop.
+  tip_339: /platforms shows gateway and messaging-platform connection status right from inside chat.
+  tip_340: /commands paginates the full slash-command + installed-skill list — useful on platforms without tab completion.
+  tip_341: /toolsets lists every available toolset so you know what -t/--toolsets accepts.
+  tip_342: /voice tts toggles TTS-only mode — agent replies out loud but you still type your prompts.
+  tip_343: /reload-skills re-scans ~/.hermes/skills/ so drop-in skills appear without restarting the session.
+  tip_344: /indicator kaomoji|emoji|unicode|ascii picks the TUI busy-indicator style shown during agent runs.
+  tip_345: /debug uploads a support bundle (system info + logs) and returns shareable links — works in chat too.
+  tip_346: 'hermes -z "<prompt>" is the purest one-shot: final answer on stdout, nothing else — ideal for piping in scripts.'
+  tip_347: hermes chat --pass-session-id injects the session ID into the system prompt so the agent can self-reference it.
+  tip_348: hermes chat --image path/to/pic.png attaches a local image to a single -q query without a separate upload step.
+  tip_349: hermes chat --ignore-user-config skips the active user config — reproducible bug reports and CI runs.
+  tip_350: hermes chat --source tool tags programmatic chats so they don't clutter hermes sessions list.
+  tip_351: hermes dump --show-keys includes redacted API key fingerprints for deeper support debugging.
+  tip_352: hermes sessions rename <ID> "new title" renames any past session; hermes sessions delete <ID> removes one.
+  tip_353: hermes import restores a full Hermes backup zip; session JSON/JSONL exports import from the dashboard Sessions page.
+  tip_354: hermes fallback manages the fallback_model chain interactively — no hand-editing config.yaml.
+  tip_355: hermes pairing rotates the DM pairing token — the first messager after rotation claims access to the bot.
+  tip_356: hermes setup walks first-time users through provider, keys, and platform wiring in one interactive flow.
+  tip_357: hermes status --deep runs the full health sweep across every component; plain hermes status is the quick view.
+  tip_358: HERMES_AGENT_TIMEOUT=0 disables the gateway inactivity kill for a running agent — use for long research runs.
+  tip_359: HERMES_ENABLE_PROJECT_PLUGINS=1 auto-loads repo-local plugins from ./.hermes/plugins/ — trust-gated by design.
+  tip_360: HERMES_DISABLE_FILE_STATE_GUARD=1 turns off the 'file changed since you read it' guard on patch and write_file.
+  tip_361: HERMES_ALLOW_PRIVATE_URLS=true lets web tools hit localhost and private networks — off by default in gateway mode.
+  tip_362: HERMES_OPTIONAL_SKILLS=name1,name2 auto-installs extra optional-catalog skills on first run per profile.
+  tip_363: HERMES_BUNDLED_SKILLS points at a custom bundled-skill tree — used by Homebrew and Nix packaging.
+  tip_364: HERMES_DUMP_REQUEST_STDOUT=1 dumps every API request payload to stdout instead of log files.
+  tip_365: HERMES_OAUTH_TRACE=1 logs redacted OAuth token exchange and refresh attempts for debugging provider auth.
+  tip_366: HERMES_STREAM_RETRIES (default 3) controls mid-stream reconnect attempts on transient network errors.
+  tip_367: HERMES_GATEWAY_BUSY_ACK_ENABLED=false silences the ⚡/⏳/⏩ ack messages when a user messages a busy agent.
+  tip_368: HERMES_AGENT_NOTIFY_INTERVAL (default 180s) sets how often the gateway pings with progress on long turns.
+  tip_369: HERMES_RESTART_DRAIN_TIMEOUT (default 900s) caps how long /restart waits for in-flight runs before forcing.
+  tip_370: HERMES_CHECKPOINT_TIMEOUT (default 30s) caps filesystem checkpoint creation — raise it on huge monorepos.
+  tip_371: 'image_gen.model in config.yaml picks the FAL model: flux-2/klein, gpt-image-2, nano-banana-pro, and more.'
+  tip_372: image_gen.provider routes image generation through a plugin (OpenAI Images, Codex, FAL) instead of the default.
+  tip_373: AUXILIARY_VISION_BASE_URL + AUXILIARY_VISION_API_KEY point vision analysis at any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
+  tip_374: 'security.tirith_fail_open: false makes Hermes block commands when the tirith scanner itself errors out.'
+  tip_375: TIRITH_FAIL_OPEN env var overrides the tirith_fail_open config — a quick toggle without editing config.yaml.
+  tip_376: --source tool chats are excluded from hermes sessions list by default — set --source explicitly to see them.
+  tip_377: Session IDs are timestamp-prefixed (20250305_091523_abcd) so sorting works naturally in ls and jq.
+  tip_378: API_SERVER_MODEL_NAME customizes the model name on /v1/models — essential for multi-profile Open WebUI setups.
+  tip_379: Dashboard plugins are served from /dashboard-plugins/<name>/ — drop files into ~/.hermes/dashboard-plugins/.
