+  tip_220: /compress <focus topic> allocates 60-70% of the summary budget to your topic and aggressively trims the rest.
+  tip_221: On second+ compression, the compressor updates the previous summary instead of starting from scratch.
+  tip_222: Before a gateway session reset, Hermes auto-flushes important facts to memory in the background.
+  tip_223: 'network.force_ipv4: true in config.yaml fixes hangs on servers with broken IPv6 — monkey-patches socket.'
+  tip_224: 'The terminal tool annotates common exit codes: grep returning 1 = ''No matches found (not an error)''.'
+  tip_225: Failed foreground terminal commands auto-retry up to 3 times with exponential backoff (2s, 4s, 8s).
+  tip_226: Bare sudo commands are auto-rewritten to pipe SUDO_PASSWORD from .env — no interactive prompt needed.
+  tip_227: 'execute_code helpers require explicit imports: from hermes_tools import json_parse, shell_quote, retry.'
+  tip_228: execute_code's 7 sandbox tools (web_search, terminal, read/write/search/patch) use RPC — never enter context.
+  tip_229: Reading the same file region 3+ times triggers a warning. At 4+, it's hard-blocked to prevent loops.
+  tip_230: write_file and patch detect if a file was externally modified since the last read and warn about staleness.
+  tip_231: V4A patch format supports Add File, Delete File, and Move File directives — not just Update.
+  tip_232: MCP servers can request LLM completions back via sampling — the agent becomes a tool for the server.
+  tip_233: MCP servers send notifications/tools/list_changed to trigger automatic tool re-registration without restart.
+  tip_234: 'delegate_task with acp_command: ''claude'' spawns Claude Code as a child agent from any platform.'
+  tip_235: Delegation has a heartbeat thread — child activity propagates to the parent, preventing gateway timeouts.
+  tip_236: When a provider returns HTTP 402 (payment required), the auxiliary client auto-falls back to the next one.
+  tip_237: agent.tool_use_enforcement steers models that describe actions instead of calling tools — auto for GPT/Codex.
+  tip_238: agent.restart_after_turn_timeout lets in-flight turns finish before /restart enters stop(); restart_drain_timeout is only the force-interrupt budget once stop() begins.
+  tip_239: agent.api_max_retries (default 3) controls how many times the agent retries a failed API call before surfacing the error — lower it for fast fallback.
+  tip_240: The gateway caches AIAgent instances per session — destroying this cache breaks Anthropic prompt caching.
+  tip_241: Any website can expose skills via /.well-known/skills/index.json — the skills hub discovers them automatically.
+  tip_242: The skills audit log at ~/.hermes/skills/.hub/audit.log tracks every install and removal operation.
+  tip_243: 'Stale git worktrees are auto-cleaned on startup: clean, fully-merged trees get pruned; dirty or unpushed work is always preserved.'
